---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SuperstockLab from "../../components/SuperstockLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Superstock Problem"
  description="Most individual stocks lose to Treasury bills; a tiny few create all the market's wealth. See why hand-picking a few stocks usually underperforms."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>Why a few stocks do all the work</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      "How Many Stocks?" showed diversification smooths the ride. This is the
      deeper, stranger reason to own lots of them. Research by Hendrik
      Bessembinder found that <strong>most individual stocks actually lose to
      Treasury bills</strong> over their lifetime — and nearly all of the stock
      market's wealth comes from a tiny handful of runaway winners. Miss those,
      and you lose.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <SuperstockLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Skewness, and the superstocks</h2>
      <p>
        Stock returns aren't a tidy bell curve. A stock can only fall 100%, but it
        can rise 1,000% or 10,000% — so the distribution is violently
        <strong>right-skewed</strong>. The <em>median</em> stock is mediocre or a
        loser; the <em>average</em> is dragged upward by a few enormous winners
        like the Apples and Amazons. In Bessembinder's data, just the top
        handful of companies accounted for the majority of all net wealth created.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The math of missing.</strong> If a few percent of stocks drive
          everything, a portfolio of five or ten names probably doesn't contain
          one of them. So your <em>typical</em> outcome lands below the market —
          even though the market's average is great.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Concentration cuts both ways — badly.</strong> It's not just
          more volatile; it's tilted so the likely result is underperformance,
          with a small chance of a jackpot. That's a lottery, not an edge.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The fix is to own them all.</strong> Index the whole market and
          you're guaranteed to hold every superstock. You give up the jackpot
          dream, but you capture the returns that actually show up.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This is a simulation calibrated to illustrate the shape of Bessembinder's
        result — not exact historical returns. Educational only, not advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextTool current="/tools/superstocks" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .sk-quicks {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .sk-quicks .wl-btn {
    flex: 1;
  }
  .sk-reseed {
    width: 100%;
  }
  .sk-ustats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.1rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .sk-ustats strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .sk-headline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
  .sk-headline-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .sk-headline-value {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .sk-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .sk-stats > div {
    min-width: 0;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .sk-stats dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .sk-stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
